en:{project:'Project',explore:'Explore',method:'Data & methods',chapter:'URBAN DESIGN PORTFOLIO / STUDY 01',title:'KAJICHO',subtitle:'WIND. LIGHT. CARBON.',intro:'Explore how trees, buildings and energy choices change the same city block.',place:'Tokyo · Kajicho 1 & 2',course:'URBAN DESIGN STUDIO / THEME B',model:'Real PLATEAU geometry',edition:'PARAMETER STUDIES / 02',wind:'Wind',shade:'Shade',carbon:'Carbon',before:'Baseline',after:'Your proposal',baseline:'FIXED BASELINE',proposal:'SCENARIO',viewReset:'Reset view',topView:'Top view',pause:'Pause',play:'Play',viewHint:'Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom · Select a building',scenario:'Build a scenario',preset:'Starting point',custom:'Custom',existing:'Existing conditions',green:'Street shade',mixed:'Shade + energy',direction:'Wind from',treeCount:'Added crowns',radius:'Crown radius',treeHeight:'Crown center height',season:'Season date',hour:'Local time',height:'Core building height',eui:'Annual electricity use',saving:'Energy saving',pv:'Self-use solar share',factor:'Electricity carbon factor',spring:'Spring · March 21',summer:'Summer · July 15',winter:'Winter · December 21',windScope:'Crown count, radius and direction select separate IIS flow runs.',shadeScope:'Height scales proposal buildings in the core. Crowns update the ground shade.',carbonScope:'Solar share applies to demand after energy saving. Values cover operational purchased electricity.',display:'Display',opacity:'Building opacity',speed:'Animation speed',field:'Ground layer',absolute:'Speed',difference:'Difference',contrast:'Difference contrast',displayNote:'Display controls do not change calculated results.',baselineValue:'Baseline',proposalValue:'Proposal',windMetric:'Mean relative speed in the core',shadeMetric:'Shaded open ground',carbonMetric:'Assumed annual electricity carbon',change:'Change from baseline',pp:'percentage points',unitTrees:'crowns',save:'Export scenario',reset:'Reset inputs',loading:'Loading a calculated scenario…',error:'The scenario could not load. Refresh to try again.',inspect:'Building details',pick:'Select a building',pickText:'Read its source height, floors and electricity scenario.',heightLabel:'Height',levels:'Floors',area:'Model plan area',source:'Source',estimated:'Estimated',unknown:'Unknown',survey:'Survey year',core:'Core area',context:'Context building',electricity:'Assumed annual carbon',sourceUse:'Source use',aboutTitle:'One block. Three studies.',aboutText:'Compare planning variables on a shared city model. Read spatial changes, then identify the data and checks that a proposal needs.',siteTitle:'The site',siteText:'1,981 real buildings. The draft core boundary follows the 2020 census areas of Kajicho 1 & 2. It contains internal points of 277 buildings.',variablesTitle:'What can change',variablesText:'Start with 8 wind directions, 0 / 24 / 48 crowns and 3 radii. Explore seasons, hours, building height and electricity assumptions.',evidenceTitle:'Reading the result',evidenceText:'Wind uses simplified 2D flow. Shade uses geometric sampling. Carbon uses electricity scenarios. Color, opacity and playback have separate controls.',methodsTitle:'Data & computation',close:'Close',buildingMethod:'Buildings / PLATEAU 2025 release, mainly surveyed in 2021. Source LOD1 plan outlines are extruded by height. 1,928 heights come from source attributes and 53 from model geometry. CRS: EPSG:6677, with flat local ground.',windMethod:'Wind / 56 D2Q9 flow cases were computed on IIS. The 2D model uses a 5 m grid, periodic boundaries and constant forcing. Each run has 4,500 steps; the final 500 are averaged. Crown drag is fixed at 0.006. Both views use the baseline 90th-percentile speed for that direction as the reference. Relative speeds are not calibrated to observed m/s.',shadeMethod:'Shade / Solar rays are traced through the 5 m building height grid. Proposed spherical crowns cast geometric shadows. Existing trees have not been surveyed; baseline shade contains buildings only. Ground shade does not give air-temperature change. The height factor affects core buildings in the Shade view only.',carbonMethod:'Carbon / Plan area × floors × assumed electricity intensity × carbon factor. Energy saving is applied first, then self-use solar. Solar has zero direct use-stage emissions here; equipment life-cycle emissions are outside this calculation. The default factor is 0.421 kg CO₂/kWh. Edited values are scenario assumptions. Actual building use, local exhaust and waste heat await field data.',planningMethod:'Proposal / Candidate crowns sit near mapped roads. Counts 0 / 24 / 48 share a nested sequence. Radius and center height are assumptions. Planting space, traffic, fire access and buried services require site checks.',dataLink:'Source record',checksLink:'Flow checks',plateauLink:'PLATEAU data',factorLink:'Carbon factor source',credits:'PLATEAU / MLIT · © OpenStreetMap contributors · Census 2020',windNote:'{count} separate numerical cases · relative speed',shadeNote:'{date} · {hour}:00 JST · {cells} open-ground cells',carbonNote:'Floor-area proxy {area} m² · assumed electricity',windLegend:'Relative speed / shared scale',differenceLegend:'Proposal − baseline / relative speed',shadeLegend:'Shade / sun',carbonLegend:'Assumed building carbon / t CO₂/year',windExplanation:'The difference map subtracts baseline from proposal. Negative values mean lower speed. Contrast changes the color range only.',shadeExplanation:'Crowns and building height both change ground shade. The baseline keeps source buildings; existing trees await a survey.',carbonExplanation:'Buildings show assumed annual electricity carbon. Indirect electricity emissions are separate from local street-level sources.',treeSummary:'{count} added crowns · {radius} m radius',windSmall:'Speed changes are small in this model. Use Difference to inspect their location.',perYear:'/year',floor:'floors',north:'N',northeast:'NE',east:'E',southeast:'SE',south:'S',southwest:'SW',west:'W',northwest:'NW',baselineFixed:'Baseline shares direction, season and electricity intensity. Proposal controls affect the right-hand view.',keyHint:'Crowns: wind + shade · Height: shade · Savings + solar: carbon',light:'Sun',shadow:'Shade',unknownUsage:'Building'},
